From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdi32: keep Uniscribe's font cache list whole when threads race

Purpose: XP Explorer no longer freezes when several of its folder windows
redraw at once, as they do when a drive goes (Eject of a disc image).
Windows behavior: Uniscribe may be used from several threads at a time.
Wine before: init_script_cache looks the font up, makes a cache outside the
lock, puts it on the list and then looks again for one another thread made
meanwhile. When it found one, it took that other cache off the list and freed
its own, which stayed on the list. Later lookups walked freed memory while
holding the lock: an access violation, which in a window procedure is caught,
left the lock held, and every other thread that draws text waited for it for
ever.
Change: the second lookup comes first, and the new cache is put on the list
only when there is no other; otherwise it is freed.
Evidence: tests/uniscribe-thread.c crashed or hung in six of six runs without
the patch. On the EeePC an Eject with two folder windows open froze My
Computer: two access violations in one Explorer thread, then another waiting
for "usp10.c: script_cache".
Scope: all programs.
---
 dlls/gdi32/uniscribe/usp10.c | 18 +++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/gdi32/uniscribe/usp10.c b/dlls/gdi32/uniscribe/usp10.c
index 43afbaa..e6152f1 100644
--- a/dlls/gdi32/uniscribe/usp10.c
+++ b/dlls/gdi32/uniscribe/usp10.c
@@ -778,7 +778,7 @@ static inline BOOL set_cache_glyph_widths(SCRIPT_CACHE *psc, WORD glyph, ABC *ab
 
 static HRESULT init_script_cache(const HDC hdc, SCRIPT_CACHE *psc)
 {
-    ScriptCache *sc;
+    ScriptCache *sc, *other;
     unsigned size;
     LOGFONTW lf;
 
@@ -828,23 +828,23 @@ static HRESULT init_script_cache(const HDC hdc, SCRIPT_CACHE *psc)
     }
     sc->lf = lf;
     sc->refcount = 1;
-    *psc = sc;
 
     EnterCriticalSection(&cs_script_cache);
-    list_add_head(&script_cache_list, &sc->entry);
-    LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(sc, &script_cache_list, ScriptCache, entry)
+    LIST_FOR_EACH_ENTRY(other, &script_cache_list, ScriptCache, entry)
     {
-        if (sc != *psc && !memcmp(&sc->lf, &lf, sizeof(lf)))
+        if (!memcmp(&other->lf, &lf, sizeof(lf)))
         {
             /* Another thread won the race. Use their cache instead of ours */
-            list_remove(&sc->entry);
-            sc->refcount++;
+            other->refcount++;
             LeaveCriticalSection(&cs_script_cache);
-            free(*psc);
-            *psc = sc;
+            free(sc->otm);
+            free(sc);
+            *psc = other;
             return S_OK;
         }
     }
+    list_add_head(&script_cache_list, &sc->entry);
+    *psc = sc;
     LeaveCriticalSection(&cs_script_cache);
     TRACE("<- %p\n", sc);
     return S_OK;
